ng a Kinotic App, defining an entity, generating its repository, and using the repository to read and write data.",[228,229,231],"h2",{"id":230},"prerequisites","Prerequisites",[233,234,235,249],"ul",{},[236,237,238,242,243],"li",{},[239,240,241],"strong",{},"Bun"," -- Install from ",[244,245,246],"a",{"href":246,"rel":247},"https:\u002F\u002Fbun.sh",[248],"nofollow",[236,250,251,254],{},[239,252,253],{},"A Kinotic account"," with a linked GitHub organization",[228,256,258],{"id":257},"create-your-application","Create Your Application",[224,260,261],{},"Kinotic OS creates your Application and Project and provisions a GitHub repository for it, already scaffolded as a Bun workspace with the Kinotic CLI vendored as a dev dependency -- there is nothing to install globally.",[224,263,264],{},"The fastest way is the official Claude Code plugin, which drives the whole flow conversationally:",[266,267,272],"pre",{"className":268,"code":270,"language":271},[269],"language-text","\u002Fplugin marketplace add kinotic-ai\u002Fclaude-plugin\n\u002Fplugin install kinotic@kinotic\n\u002Fkinotic:new-app my-app\n","text",[273,274,270],"code",{"__ignoreMap":275},"",[224,277,278],{},"You can also create the Application and Project from the Kinotic OS dashboard; either way you end up with a provisioned repository.",[228,280,282],{"id":281},"clone-and-install","Clone and Install",[266,284,288],{"className":285,"code":286,"language":287,"meta":275,"style":275},"language-bash shiki shiki-themes material-theme-lighter material-theme material-theme-palenight","git clone \u003Cyour-provisioned-repo> && cd \u003Cyour-repo>\nbun install\n","bash",[273,289,290,334],{"__ignoreMap":275},[291,292,295,299,303,307,310,314,317,320,324,326,329,331],"span",{"class":293,"line":294},"line",1,[291,296,298],{"class":297},"sBMFI","git",[291,300,302],{"class":301},"sfazB"," clone",[291,304,306],{"class":305},"sMK4o"," \u003C",[291,308,309],{"class":301},"your-provisioned-rep",[291,311,313],{"class":312},"sTE